          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Genetic engineering is a modern method for producing crop plants with improved characteristics.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "One example of a crop plant with improved characteristics is soybean, <i>Glycine</i> <i>max</i>, which has been genetically modified to make it resistant to a herbicide. This genetically modified soybean is called GM soybean.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "To create GM soybean, a bacterial gene and a section of regulatory DNA were introduced into soybean cells.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Outline the roles of enzymes and a section of regulatory DNA in the creation of genetically modified organisms such as GM soybean.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "marks": 5,
        "topics": [
